/-!
# Finite presentation of the quotient of the structure sheaf by a finite-type ideal

Let `R` be a sheaf of rings on a site and let `𝓘 ⊆ 𝒪` be a sub-`𝒪`-module of the structure
sheaf, that is, a sheaf of ideals.  If `𝓘` is of finite type then the quotient `𝒪/𝓘` is of
finite presentation: over a member of a covering on which `𝓘` is generated by `n` sections, the
quotient is presented by the one generator `1` and the `n` relations given by those sections.

Applied to the defining ideal sheaf of a closed subspace `Z ⊆ X` of an algebraic space, and
combined with the identification `𝒪_X/𝓘_Z ≅ i_*𝒪_Z` of Stacks 09RP in degree zero, this says
that `i_*𝒪_Z` is an `𝒪_X`-module of finite presentation as soon as `𝓘_Z` is of finite type.

This is the module half of the dictionary used by Stacks 0D00 to identify the Hilbert functor of
`X/B` with the Quot functor of `𝒪_X/X/B`; the geometric half, comparing finite presentation of
`Z ⟶ T` with finite presentation of the closed immersion `i`, is
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.isFinitePresentation_comp_iff_of_isClosedImmersion`.

## Main results

* `Stacks.SheafOfModules.surjective_factorThruImage_val_app_of_mono`: a monomorphism of sheaves
  of modules is, on the sections over any object, surjective onto its image.
* `Stacks.SheafOfModules.hasFiniteGlobalPresentation_over_cokernel_of_mono_unit`: if a sheaf of
  ideals is generated by finitely many sections over an object, the quotient of the structure
  sheaf by it has a finite global presentation on the slice over that object.
* `Stacks.SheafOfModules.isFinitePresentationOnSite_cokernel_of_mono_unit`: **the quotient of
  the structure sheaf by a sheaf of ideals of finite type is of finite presentation.**
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.isFinitePresentationOnSite_cokernel_definingIdealSheaf` and
  `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.isFinitePresentationOnSite_pushforwardStructureSheaf`: the same for
  the defining ideal sheaf of a closed subspace of an algebraic space, in the two forms
  `𝒪_X/𝓘_Z` and `i_*𝒪_Z`.

## Implementation notes

The presentation is produced through the sections criterion
`SheafOfModules.hasFiniteGlobalPresentation_over_of_generates`, not by manipulating cokernels of
coproducts.  The reason is that a cokernel of sheaves of modules is a sheafification, so the
restriction of `𝒪/𝓘` to a slice site is not the cokernel of the restricted inclusion on the nose
and transporting the universal property across that comparison is more work than reading the
presentation off sections.  The three inputs the criterion asks for are:

* that the single section `1` of `𝒪/𝓘` generate it locally, which is local surjectivity of the
  projection, that is `Stacks.SheafOfModules.EpiMono.exists_covering_of_epi` applied to the
  epimorphism `CategoryTheory.Limits.cokernel.π`;
* that the chosen generators of `𝓘` be relations, which is `cokernel.condition`;
* that they generate all relations locally, which is exactness of
  `𝓘 ⟶ 𝒪 ⟶ 𝒪/𝓘` on the sections over each object followed by the generation hypothesis.

The last of these is where the hypothesis that the inclusion be a *monomorphism* is used, and it
is the only place.  Sections of sheaves of modules are left exact but not right exact, so
`SheafOfModules.exact_val_app_cokernel_π` carries the surjectivity of the canonical epimorphism
onto the image as a hypothesis; for a monomorphism that epimorphism is an isomorphism, so the
hypothesis is free.  This is the same observation that `him` is discharged by in
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.isQuasicoherentOnSite_cokernel_definingIdealSheaf`.

No tag attribute is placed.  Stacks 03DL(7) is already registered on
`SheafOfModules.IsFinitePresentationOnSite`, and what is proved here is a sufficient criterion
for it rather than a part of that tag; the geometric corollaries are inputs to Stacks 0D00 and
not clauses of it.  This follows the convention of the sibling file
`StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/Spaces/ClosedSubspaceQuotientQuasicoherent.lean`.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 03DE](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/03DE)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 03DL](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/03DL)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 09RP](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/09RP)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0D00](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0D00)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits Opposite SheafOfModules

universe u v w

namespace Stacks.SheafOfModules

variable {C : Type u} [Category.{v} C] {J : GrothendieckTopology C} {R : Sheaf J RingCat.{w}}
  [HasSheafify J AddCommGrpCat.{w}] [J.WEqualsLocallyBijective AddCommGrpCat.{w}]

/-- **A monomorphism of sheaves of modules is surjective onto its image on the sections over
every object.**  The canonical epimorphism of a monomorphism onto its image is a monomorphism
too, hence an isomorphism, and an isomorphism of sheaves of modules is bijective on sections
because evaluation at an object is a functor. -/
theorem surjective_factorThruImage_val_app_of_mono {M N : _root_.SheafOfModules.{w} R}
    (φ : M ⟶ N) [Mono φ] (U : Cᵒᵖ) :
    Function.Surjective ((Abelian.factorThruImage φ).val.app U) := by
  have hiso : IsIso (Abelian.factorThruImage φ) := isIso_of_mono_of_epi _
  let e : M ≅ Abelian.image φ := ⟨Abelian.factorThruImage φ, inv (Abelian.factorThruImage φ),
    IsIso.hom_inv_id _, IsIso.inv_hom_id _⟩
  let e' := (_root_.SheafOfModules.evaluation R U).mapIso e
  have : IsIso ((_root_.SheafOfModules.evaluation R U).map (Abelian.factorThruImage φ)) :=
    ⟨e'.inv, e'.hom_inv_id, e'.inv_hom_id⟩
  exact (ConcreteCategory.bijective_of_isIso
    ((_root_.SheafOfModules.evaluation R U).map (Abelian.factorThruImage φ))).2

/-- Restricting the image of `1` in `𝒪/𝓘` along `g` gives the image of `1` over the source. -/
private theorem restrict_cokernel_π_unitOf_one {M : _root_.SheafOfModules.{w} R}
    (φ : M ⟶ _root_.SheafOfModules.unit R) {Y V : C} (g : Y ⟶ V) :
    (cokernel φ).val.restrictₛₗ g.op
        ((cokernel.π φ).val.app (op V) (unitOf (1 : R.obj.obj (op V)))) =
      (cokernel.π φ).val.app (op Y) (unitOf (1 : R.obj.obj (op Y))) := by
  rw [← PresheafOfModules.unit_map_one R.obj g.op]
  exact (PresheafOfModules.naturality_apply (cokernel.π φ).val g.op _).symm

/-- **A finite global presentation of the quotient of the structure sheaf by a sheaf of ideals
generated by finitely many sections.**  Let `φ : 𝓘 ⟶ 𝒪` be a monomorphism of sheaves of modules
into the structure sheaf and let `V` be an object over which `𝓘` is generated by finitely many
global sections.  Then the quotient `𝒪/𝓘` has a finite global presentation on the slice site
over `V`: one generator, the image of `1`, and one relation for each of the chosen generators of
`𝓘`.

Generation by the image of `1` is local surjectivity of the projection; that the generators of
`𝓘` are relations is the defining property of the cokernel; and that they generate all relations
locally is exactness of `𝓘 ⟶ 𝒪 ⟶ 𝒪/𝓘` on sections, available because `φ` is a monomorphism,
followed by the generation hypothesis. -/
theorem hasFiniteGlobalPresentation_over_cokernel_of_mono_unit
    {M : _root_.SheafOfModules.{w} R} (φ : M ⟶ _root_.SheafOfModules.unit R) [Mono φ] (V : C)
    (h : (M.over V).HasFiniteGlobalGenerators) :
    ((cokernel φ).over V).HasFiniteGlobalPresentation := by
  obtain ⟨n, g, hgen⟩ := exists_generates_of_hasFiniteGlobalGenerators_over M V h
  have hsurj (U : Cᵒᵖ) : Function.Surjective ((Abelian.factorThruImage φ).val.app U) :=
    surjective_factorThruImage_val_app_of_mono φ U
  have hexact (U : Cᵒᵖ) :
      Function.Exact (φ.val.app U) ((cokernel.π φ).val.app U) :=
    _root_.SheafOfModules.exact_val_app_cokernel_π φ U (hsurj U)
  have hzero : φ ≫ cokernel.π φ = 0 := cokernel.condition φ
  -- acting on `1` by a ring element `a` gives the section `a`
  have smul_unitOf_one {U : Cᵒᵖ} (a : R.obj.obj U) :
      (a • unitOf (1 : R.obj.obj U) : (_root_.SheafOfModules.unit R).val.obj U) = unitOf a := by
    rw [_root_.SheafOfModules.unit_smul]
    exact congrArg unitOf (mul_one _)
  -- the generator of the quotient over `V` and the relations coming from the generators of `𝓘`
  refine _root_.SheafOfModules.hasFiniteGlobalPresentation_over_of_generates (cokernel φ) V
    (n := 1) (p := n)
    (fun _ ↦ (cokernel.π φ).val.app (op V) (unitOf (1 : R.obj.obj (op V))))
    (fun k _ ↦ unitVal (φ.val.app (op V) (g k))) ?_ ?_ ?_
  · intro k
    rw [Fin.sum_univ_one]
    rw [← map_smul, smul_unitOf_one]
    exact congrFun (congrArg (fun ψ ↦ ⇑(ConcreteCategory.hom
      ((_root_.SheafOfModules.Hom.val ψ).app (op V)))) hzero) (g k)
  · intro W f t
    obtain ⟨T, hT, himg⟩ := EpiMono.exists_covering_of_epi (cokernel.π φ) t
    refine ⟨T, hT, fun Y p hp ↦ ?_⟩
    obtain ⟨y, hy⟩ := himg p hp
    refine ⟨fun _ ↦ unitVal y, ?_⟩
    rw [Fin.sum_univ_one]
    rw [restrict_cokernel_π_unitOf_one, ← map_smul, smul_unitOf_one]
    exact hy
  · intro W hW τ hτ
    rw [Fin.sum_univ_one] at hτ
    rw [restrict_cokernel_π_unitOf_one, ← map_smul, smul_unitOf_one] at hτ
    obtain ⟨y, hy⟩ := (hexact (op W) (unitOf (τ 0))).mp hτ
    obtain ⟨T, hT, hd⟩ := hgen W hW y
    refine ⟨T, hT, fun Y p hp ↦ ?_⟩
    obtain ⟨d, hdY⟩ := hd Y p hp
    refine ⟨d, fun i ↦ ?_⟩
    have hi : i = 0 := Subsingleton.elim i 0
    subst hi
    have hnat (k : Fin n) : φ.val.app (op Y) (M.val.map (p ≫ hW).op (g k)) =
        (_root_.SheafOfModules.unit R).val.map (p ≫ hW).op (φ.val.app (op V) (g k)) :=
      PresheafOfModules.naturality_apply φ.val (p ≫ hW).op (g k)
    have hnaty : φ.val.app (op Y) (M.val.map p.op y) =
        (_root_.SheafOfModules.unit R).val.map p.op (φ.val.app (op W) y) :=
      PresheafOfModules.naturality_apply φ.val p.op y
    have hφ := congrArg (φ.val.app (op Y)) hdY
    rw [map_sum] at hφ
    simp only [PresheafOfModules.restrictₛₗ_apply] at hφ
    rw [hnaty, hy] at hφ
    refine Eq.trans (Finset.sum_congr rfl fun k _ ↦ ?_) hφ
    refine Eq.trans (congrArg (fun z ↦ d k • z) (hnat k).symm) ?_
    exact (map_smul (ConcreteCategory.hom (φ.val.app (op Y))) (d k)
      (M.val.map (p ≫ hW).op (g k))).symm

/-- **The quotient of the structure sheaf by a sheaf of ideals of finite type is of finite
presentation.**  This is Stacks 03DL(5) implying Stacks 03DL(7) for a quotient of `𝒪`: on the
covering of an object which witnesses finite type of the ideal, the quotient has the finite
global presentation of
`Stacks.SheafOfModules.hasFiniteGlobalPresentation_over_cokernel_of_mono_unit`. -/
theorem isFinitePresentationOnSite_cokernel_of_mono_unit
    {M : _root_.SheafOfModules.{w} R} (φ : M ⟶ _root_.SheafOfModules.unit R) [Mono φ]
    (h : M.IsFiniteTypeOnSite) : (cokernel φ).IsFinitePresentationOnSite where
  locally_hasFiniteGlobalPresentation U := by
    obtain ⟨I, V, f, hcover, hgg⟩ := h.locally_finitelyGenerated U
    exact ⟨I, V, f, hcover,
      fun i ↦ hasFiniteGlobalPresentation_over_cokernel_of_mono_unit φ (V i) (hgg i)⟩

end Stacks.SheafOfModules

namespace AlgebraicGeometry.Space

variable (B : BigFppfSite.{u}) (S : Scheme.{u}) (hS : B.Contains S)
  (X : AlgebraicSpaces B S hS) (Z : ClosedSubspaces B S hS X.1)

/-- **The quotient of `𝒪_X` by the defining ideal sheaf of a closed subspace is of finite
presentation as soon as that ideal sheaf is of finite type.**

The inclusion of the defining ideal sheaf is a monomorphism, by the short exact sequence it sits
in, so this is
`Stacks.SheafOfModules.isFinitePresentationOnSite_cokernel_of_mono_unit`. -/
theorem isFinitePresentationOnSite_cokernel_definingIdealSheaf
    (hft : SheafOfModules.IsFiniteTypeOnSite
      (definingIdealSheaf B S hS X Z).toSheafOfModules) :
    (cokernel (definingIdealSheaf B S hS X Z).ι).IsFinitePresentationOnSite := by
  have hmono : Mono (definingIdealSheaf B S hS X Z).ι :=
    (definingIdealShortComplex_shortExact B S hS X Z).mono_f
  exact Stacks.SheafOfModules.isFinitePresentationOnSite_cokernel_of_mono_unit
    (definingIdealSheaf B S hS X Z).ι hft

/-- **The direct image of the structure sheaf of a closed subspace is an `𝒪_X`-module of finite
presentation as soon as the defining ideal sheaf is of finite type.**  For a closed subspace
`Z ⊆ X` with inclusion `i`, the module `i_*𝒪_Z` is the quotient `𝒪_X/𝓘_Z` by Stacks 09RP in
degree zero, available as `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.conormalAlgebraDegreeZeroIso`, and finite
presentation is invariant under isomorphism.

Together with Stacks 084Q — finite presentation of the closed immersion `i` is finite type of
`𝓘_Z` — and with
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.isFinitePresentation_comp_iff_of_isClosedImmersion`, this is the
finite-presentation entry of the dictionary of Stacks 0D00 between a family classified by the
Hilbert functor and the quotient of the structure sheaf it determines. -/
@[ega "IV 8.6.1" "partial"]
theorem isFinitePresentationOnSite_pushforwardStructureSheaf
    (hft : SheafOfModules.IsFiniteTypeOnSite
      (definingIdealSheaf B S hS X Z).toSheafOfModules) :
    (pushforwardStructureSheaf B S hS X Z).IsFinitePresentationOnSite :=
  SheafOfModules.IsFinitePresentationOnSite.of_iso
    (conormalAlgebraDegreeZeroIso B S hS X Z)
    (isFinitePresentationOnSite_cokernel_definingIdealSheaf B S hS X Z hft)

/-- **The finite-presentation entry of the dictionary of Stacks 0D00, forward direction.**  Let
`p : X ⟶ T` be a morphism of algebraic spaces over `S` of finite presentation and let
`Z ⊆ X` be a closed subspace with inclusion `i`.  If `Z ⟶ T` is of finite presentation, then the
quotient `𝒪_X ⟶ i_*𝒪_Z` it determines is a module of finite presentation.

The source's chain is run in order: `Z ⟶ T` and `X ⟶ T` of finite presentation give that `i` is,
which is
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.isFinitePresentation_of_comp_of_isClosedImmersion`; finite presentation
of a closed immersion is finite type of its ideal sheaf, which is Stacks 084Q; and finite type of
the ideal sheaf gives finite presentation of the quotient, which is
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.isFinitePresentationOnSite_pushforwardStructureSheaf`.

The hypothesis `hchart` is the one input of Stacks 084Q which the library does not supply, in the
form
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.isFinitePresentation_iff_isFiniteTypeOnSite_kernelIdealSheaf_of_chart`
consumes it: the comparison, at a surjective étale scheme chart of `X`, of finite type of the
ideal sheaf on the small étale site with finite generation of the chart-level ideal over the
affine opens of that chart.

The converse direction needs that a quotient of `𝒪_X` of finite presentation has an ideal sheaf
of finite type, which is Modules on Sites, Lemma 18.24.2 — that is, Stacks 082T, which is
`Stacks.SheafOfModules.SliceFinite.isFiniteType_kernel_of_epi`.  Applied to the short exact
sequence of Stacks 09RP in degree zero it is
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.isFiniteTypeOnSite_definingIdealSheaf_of_isFinitePresentationOnSite`. -/
theorem isFinitePresentationOnSite_pushforwardStructureSheaf_of_isFinitePresentation
    {T : AlgebraicSpaces B S hS} (p : X ⟶ T) (hp : IsFinitePresentation B S hS p.hom)
    (hchart : ∀ (V : BigFppfOver B S hS) (b : yoneda.obj V ⟶ X.1),
      (MorphismProperty.inverseImage
        (@_root_.AlgebraicGeometry.Etale.{u} : MorphismProperty Scheme.{u})
        (BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS)).presheaf b →
      (MorphismProperty.inverseImage
        (@_root_.AlgebraicGeometry.Surjective.{u} : MorphismProperty Scheme.{u})
        (BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS)).presheaf b →
      (SheafOfModules.IsFiniteTypeOnSite
          (kernelIdealSheaf B S hS (subspaceInclusion B S hS X Z)).toSheafOfModules ↔
        ∀ A : ((BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).obj V).affineOpens,
          (((BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).map (Z.2.2.rep.snd b)).ker.ideal A).FG))
    (hZT : IsFinitePresentation B S hS ((subspaceInclusion B S hS X Z).hom ≫ p.hom)) :
    (pushforwardStructureSheaf B S hS X Z).IsFinitePresentationOnSite := by
  have hi : IsFinitePresentation B S hS (subspaceInclusion B S hS X Z).hom :=
    isFinitePresentation_of_comp_of_isClosedImmersion B S hS Z.2.1 X.property T.property
      (subspaceInclusion B S hS X Z).hom p.hom Z.2.2
      (isLocallyOfFiniteType_of_isLocallyOfFinitePresentation B S hS hp.1) hZT
  refine isFinitePresentationOnSite_pushforwardStructureSheaf B S hS X Z ?_
  rw [← kernelIdealSheaf_eq_definingIdealSheaf B S hS X Z]
  exact (isFinitePresentation_iff_isFiniteTypeOnSite_kernelIdealSheaf_of_chart B S hS
    (subspaceInclusion B S hS X Z) Z.2.2 hchart).mp hi

end AlgebraicGeometry.Space

end
